    "essay": [
      [
        "There has been a fierce yet unresolved debate as to what **roles** males and females **should play** in **society.**",
        "With **perceived differences** in physical ability comes the belief that women are ill-equipped to work in the police force or the army, whereas others insist that women **can be** as capable as their male counterparts in such professions.",
        "Both views are discussed here to seek a conclusion."
      ],
      [
        "The argument against women serving in the military **or** law enforcement agencies **rests on concerns** that **some** duties **may be** too **physically** demanding for **them** to qualify.",
        "Unlike **many less physically demanding jobs,** being a soldier or a sworn officer **can require** applicants to be tough and strong physically and mentally, **standards that critics believe some** female candidates **may struggle** to **meet.**",
        "These traits enable **applicants** to pass **physical** fitness assessments, endure **rotating** shift work, and **help protect** their safety when they are confronted with criminals or hostile forces.",
        "Therefore, **applicants** who **do not meet the relevant standards, regardless of gender,** are not **suitable** for these **particular duties; this does not establish that women as a group are unsuitable.**"
      ],
      [
        "Others, however, highlight the **important role that** females **can play in** the police force.",
        "**Day-to-day** policing **includes** community-oriented **work,** and in an institution designed to serve communities, **many tasks rely on judgement and communication as well as** physical **fitness, so** women can function and perform as well as men **do, for example in** conducting interviews, patrol activities, and traffic **investigations.**",
        "In view of the **importance of being** approachable, sympathetic, and communicative, female officers **who possess these qualities** can greatly contribute to the relationship between police departments and communities."
      ],
      [
        "With regard to the military, **soldiers do not always** get involved in armed conflicts **or** have to undertake **combat duties.**",
        "Even though disparities **in average** physical **strength exist,** the gender gap in performing **some** military duties **may be narrowed by** the development of **weapons and equipment.**",
        "The success of a war or a battle **rests not only on stamina and physical fitness but also** on tactics and **strategies.**",
        "Such requirements justify the role of females, be they in the army, navy or **air force,** as **gender alone does not determine an individual's intellectual ability.**"
      ],
      [
        "In conclusion, even though gender **differences may exist** in terms of **average** physical **strength,** females can **play,** and **already play,** a central role in policing and **the armed forces, given the range of responsibilities in these occupations** and the **individual abilities they require.**"
      ]
    ],
