    "essay": [
      [
        "Efforts have always been made to improve gender equality from generation to generation; some workplaces are adopting a policy whereby equal numbers of men and women should be employed.",
        "Although it seemingly manifests improved gender equality, it can be used as a cover for **continuing inequality, which makes reliance on numerical equality a negative development in my view.**"
      ],
      [
        "The argument **in** favour of this equal-number policy is that it can **help** tackle gender inequality in employment.",
        "A gender stereotype in the workplace exists, whereby female employees **are sometimes** perceived as less capable and less **assertive** than their male counterparts; therefore, **some employers tend** to place a premium on male candidates.",
        "However, with this policy, female candidates can get more job opportunities than before.",
        "For example, **occupations such as engineering, surgery,** and **dentistry could attract more female recruits where men** have **traditionally predominated,** which **could improve women’s access to these professions.**"
      ],
      [
        "However, **numerical equality alone** is **insufficient** and **can be counterproductive if it diverts attention from other barriers.**",
        "The aim of gender equality in the workplace is to achieve broadly equal opportunities and outcomes for women and men, not necessarily outcomes that are exactly the same for all.",
        "**Female** and male employees can differ in number when equal pay is offered for work of equal or comparable value; when the barriers to the full and equal participation of women in the workforce are removed; when access is provided to all occupations and industries, including leadership roles, regardless of gender; and when **discrimination** based on gender is eliminated, particularly **discrimination related to** family and caring responsibilities.",
        "Therefore, **an equal-number** policy is far from **enough,** and some companies may adopt **it while** pretending that they have already done their best to achieve **gender equality.**",
        "**If this discourages further action, less visible inequalities in pay and promotion may persist.**"
      ],
      [
        "In conclusion, although this equal-number policy **can afford** more job opportunities for women, **treating** it **as sufficient** ignores what gender equality means in the workplace.",
        "More efforts are needed to truly reduce and remove inequality rather than letting it **persist behind** a **policy of** equal **numbers.**"
      ]
    ],
