    "question": "Successful sports professionals can earn a great deal more money than people in other important professions. Some people think this is fully justified while others think it is unfair. Discuss both these views and give your own opinion.",
    "essayParagraphs": [
      "Opinions differ as to the **salaries** of sports professionals. While some people think their high salaries are fully justified, others think it is unfair that they receive a great deal more money than people in other important professions (e.g., scientists and government **leaders). Both** views are discussed here to seek a **conclusion.**",
      "The argument against such high salaries for sports players is that salaries should be in proportion to the contribution individuals make to society. **Their salaries appear excessive** when **compared** with those of top surgeons, research scientists, or even leading politicians who have **responsibility for** governing the country. **From this perspective,** sports players should be paid less than those **people.**",
      "Others, however, highlight the efforts made by sports players. **The** number of professionals with **exceptional** talent is very **small,** and the money is a recognition of the skills and dedication a person needs to be successful. Competition is constant and a player is tested every time they perform in their relatively short career. The pressure from the media is intense and there is little privacy **in** the spotlight. So all of these factors may justify the huge earnings.",
      "I think sports players are **overpaid when their salaries are assessed in proportion to their social contribution.** Scientists with **exceptional** talent are also **few in number,** and they also devote time and energy to **their fields over** the long term so that they can **make** breakthroughs. For example, **an agricultural** scientist **could develop higher-yielding** rice, **improving** food security and providing a **more reliable** food **supply** in areas with a high risk of famine. **Is** pressure from the media **necessarily** more intense than the pressure **on researchers working to help communities at risk** of **hunger?** The same principle **of rewarding scarce skills, dedication and responsibility** should also apply to other important professionals.",
      "In conclusion, salaries should be based on contribution and **responsibility. The** high salaries of sports players **are difficult to justify by talent, dedication and pressure alone.** It is my opinion, therefore, that the amount of money sports stars make is **excessive when compared with the rewards received by other professionals on the basis of their social contribution.**"
    ],
