    "essay": [
      [
        "There has been a fierce yet unresolved debate as to how the government **allocates its** budget.",
        "It is proposed that the money allocated to the renovation and preservation of old buildings should be channelled into road development.",
        "Although **the demand for road development** should be met, other considerations justify the policies adopted to preserve and restore **these buildings.**"
      ],
      [
        "The argument in favour of road construction is that it can greatly contribute to city dwellers’ well-being.",
        "Many commuters are negatively **affected** by traffic, mentally and physically, especially the heavy traffic during rush hours.",
        "If more money were to be allocated to road development, ranging from the construction of flyovers to the **removal** of **traffic** bottlenecks, fewer commuters **might** complain about the experience of getting stuck in traffic for hours.",
        "**It** seems, therefore, that citizens can benefit from such reasonable budget allocation."
      ],
      [
        "However, it does not necessarily mean that there is no justification for the preservation of old buildings.",
        "**Many of these** buildings reflect the beauty of local culture and heritage.",
        "**Would** future **generations** recognize their cultural identity **as readily** if much of the physical evidence were to be erased?",
        "**Probably** not if all these old buildings disappeared and only anonymous housing estates **remained.**",
        "In addition, restored buildings can act as an economic engine, drawing tourists from all over the world.",
        "**A city,** for example, **could preserve an old** temple, capitalizing on its cultural and historic flavour to attract tourists.",
        "Therefore, the attempt to maintain such old buildings is **justifiable.**"
      ],
      [
        "Moreover, it is worthwhile to point out that if the money allocated to maintaining old buildings were to be spent on other important things (e.g., road development), the situation **might** improve **little where road infrastructure is already well developed.**",
        "This **can be explained by** the **principle** of diminishing **returns,** which **means** that as investment in a particular area increases, the **additional benefit from each unit** of **investment may decline** after a certain **point.**",
        "In **such circumstances,** the proposal **may bring only limited improvements;** by contrast, governments and citizens **can** benefit culturally from old **buildings even when their preservation is** supported by a **relatively** small proportion of the government budget."
      ],
      [
        "In conclusion, even though the high demand for road development should be satisfied, the preservation of old buildings is indispensable in view of their cultural and economic importance.",
        "**Funding for preservation** should **therefore** be maintained, **with** budget **allocations** carefully made according to a strict set of **criteria that balances transport needs with heritage protection.**"
      ]
    ],
