    "essay": [
      [
        "There has been a fierce yet unresolved debate as to how to help employees perform better at work.",
        "It is proposed by some policymakers that this goal can be achieved by entitling employees to at least four **weeks of annual leave.**",
        "Such a proposal can be regarded as an efficiency drive despite **its apparent disruption** to workflow."
      ],
      [
        "The argument in favour of this proposal is that it allows employees to reenergize and thus achieve efficiency gains at work.",
        "When employees work for too long and have no opportunities to rest and recharge themselves, problems arise: **overwork** can give rise to stress, affect mood, and **undermine** morale.",
        "**People who** suffer from work-related illnesses **may** end up resigning due to ill health; therefore, **adequate annual leave can help sustain** better performance at **work.**"
      ],
      [
        "While the justification for annual leave exists, why do people call for at least four weeks’ holiday?",
        "**Consider employees whose** annual leave entitlement is **limited to five days.**",
        "Often, **they** would use it intermittently, making **individual breaks** too short for a **sustained period of rest.**",
        "**By contrast, four weeks could allow a two-week break for sustained recovery while leaving another two weeks for shorter breaks throughout the year.**",
        "**An extended** holiday allows people to rest by doing what they are interested in (e.g., travelling to other countries) and **may** thus **help them** perform more efficiently and **be more motivated than** those who **have insufficient time to rest.**"
      ],
      [
        "However, not everyone is convinced by this efficiency measure.",
        "The critics argue that it may pose a problem to the workflow of the organization, especially when one’s **duties** can hardly be covered by others.",
        "Nonetheless, this problem can be **mitigated:** managers should **agree with** employees **on** when to **take leave and arrange cover in advance,** minimizing **disruption.**",
        "A good example **would be a company that staggers staff holidays and trains colleagues to cover essential duties; such arrangements** can **make a four-week entitlement more viable without requiring employees** to **take all their leave at once.**"
      ],
      [
        "In conclusion, although it may pose a problem to efficiency **gains** in **the short term, an entitlement to at least four weeks' holiday offers** a **reasonable minimum for combining sustained recovery with regular breaks.**",
        "**It can therefore support** better performance at **work, provided that staffing and scheduling are properly managed.**"
      ]
    ],
