    "essay": [
      [
        "**Voluntary** work **often wins** praise from others.",
        "With this comes a proposal whereby all young adults should be required to do unpaid community work.",
        "Despite its tangible benefits, **I believe the drawbacks of requiring** all young adults to **participate would be greater.**"
      ],
      [
        "The argument in favour of this policy is **that** the benefits accrue to young people themselves and the community.",
        "For young adults, they are able to experience a deep sense of satisfaction by helping others and **develop** interpersonal skills when they are interacting with local people.",
        "For the community, people living in the community **can be supported** by **these volunteers, under appropriate supervision, in obtaining** the right services when needed, be they housing support or child protection.",
        "**This can create** a **win-win situation.**"
      ],
      [
        "However, such benefits cannot justify the proposal to make community work mandatory for all.",
        "Although young adults can benefit from such community work, problems arise when a moral obligation becomes a **compulsory** requirement, which may lead to resentment: **young adults may fulfil all** the requirements but **avoid** volunteering **in future.**",
        "In addition, the community **will not necessarily** benefit more **simply because** there are more community **workers, since some** services and support **require relevant** experience or **qualifications.**",
        "**A** better option would be to **encourage** more **people,** rather than **require all,** to do unpaid community **work with suitable training.**"
      ],
      [
        "In conclusion, although intuitively young people should do unpaid community work, the proposal to **require** all to do **so risks being** counterproductive and impractical.",
        "**Its drawbacks outweigh its benefits, since voluntary participation can retain many of the gains without imposing the same obligation on unwilling participants.**",
        "**Society** should continue to call for more people to help while **allowing young adults** to volunteer of **their own** volition."
      ]
    ],
